eal is that it now gets a brand  new lidar scanner on the back for  insanely accurate depth sensing this not  only means that we should expect to get  insanely good portrait photos on the  rear camera if it supports it but it  also means that this iPad pro is going  to support the best augmented reality  we've seen on  any mobile device we know that because  lidar is actually what a bunch of  companies are using for self-driving  cars so it's the best tech out there for  depth sensing and object tracking so  those interested in augmented reality  should seriously be buying the iPad pro  for performance it now packs a new a 12  Z processing chip with an 8 core  graphics processor and a new enhanced  thermal design to make sure it stays  cool now we're not sure why it's not the  a 13 X chip maybe it means that  processing performance won't go up by  that much but if it doesn't that's okay  because the 2018 model is still overkill  for a lot of the apps on the App Store  either way we're gonna compare the  performance of the 2018 iPad pro to the  new model in just a few days when we get  our hands on it the battery on the 11  inch iPad pro is now twenty eight point  six five watt hours just slightly  smaller than the twenty nine point four  five watt hour battery in the 2018 model  but Apple is still rating it at the same  10 hours of battery life so that means  they improve the efficiency of the new  chip a huge feature is that it now  supports Wi-Fi 6 so it's going to be  future proof for a while supporting the  best Wi-Fi speeds you can get you also  get the same silver or Space Gray color  options the weight is basically the same  at just over a pound and it's exactly  the same 5.9 millimeters thick now  here's where the real magic comes in its  price at the exact same $800 but now it  comes with 128 gigs of storage twice as  much as before at the same price and the  even crazier thing is that if you  upgrade to 256 gigs of storage  it's priced at $900 whereas the 